{
  "requirement": "Listing and reading failures are errors, distinct from successful empty\nlistings and successful reads of empty resources.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.errors`.\n\nThe requirement has two obligations. Listing and reading failures must be errors, and those errors must be distinct from successful empty listings and successful reads of empty resources.\n\n**Failures are errors.** `tests/sources.rs#fn[failed_provider_operations_never_become_successful_empty_results]` uses `FailingProvider`. Its `list` fails when `list_fails` is true, and its `read` always fails. The test loops over both `list_fails` values.\n- `search_text` must return an error. The test asserts the exact message: \"listing failed\" when listing fails, otherwise \"reading failed\". A silent empty result would fail this.\n- `parse` of a resource must return the \"reading failed\" error.\n- When the `default-languages` feature is on, `search_structure` must return the same list or read error.\n\n**Empty successes are not errors.** `tests/sources.rs#fn[successful_empty_listing_and_empty_resources_are_distinct_from_errors]` uses the `Primitives` provider, again over both values of `empty_listing`.\n- `list` returns `Ok` with length 0 when `empty_listing` is true, and length 1 otherwise.\n- `read` and `parse` of an empty resource succeed and give empty bytes.\n- `search_text` returns `Ok` with `complete` true and no matches.\n- `search_structure` (under the feature) returns `Ok` with `complete` true and no matches.\n\nThis shows empty cases are successes and failures are errors.\n\n**Related checks.** `tests/sources.rs#fn[completeness_is_false_only_when_a_match_is_omitted_and_errors_propagate]` adds more evidence.\n- A bad regex makes `search_text` return an error.\n- Invalid UTF-8 bytes make `parse_snapshot` return an error.\n- An unknown language makes `parse_snapshot` return an error.\n- An empty search with `limit` 0 returns success, complete, with no matches.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests and no untested obligation. `list` and `read` failures are exercised through the SDK operations built on them, which is how the SDK surfaces them. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "f5d12103ccd0e144dacae0ddbef43dc63dc0baaf31ad27270f54575fc641203d",
